<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Expenses' cross-section surface. The leaf existed as its own project because one of its
    consumers sat in Base: HoldedExpenseOutboxJob in Humans.Infrastructure/Jobs. **That is
    no longer true** — the job moved into Humans.Expenses/Contracts/ at G5 lane 5b-5
    (nobodies-collective/Humans#866), and the only consumer left outside the section is
    Shell's AdminController, reading IExpenseReportServiceRead for the admin dashboard tile.
    Shell references Humans.Expenses directly, so a Contracts/ *folder* would now serve it.
    Left standing deliberately: collapsing a leaf is Peter's call, not a job move's side
    effect.

    Now also carries IExpenseReportServiceRead, its DTO graph (ExpenseReportDto,
    ExpenseLineDto, ExpenseAttachmentDto, ExpenseHoldedTimeline, ExpenseAttachmentDownload)
    and the two enums that graph exposes (ExpenseReportStatus, ExpenseLineType) — promoted
    for the admin dashboard tile (nobodies-collective/Humans#1264 tile wave). The section's
    own entities/mapper/repository reference these back from here rather than duplicating
    them internally.

    References Humans.Interfaces only. In particular it must not name IHoldedClient,
    HoldedPurchaseDocumentInput, HoldedAttachmentInput or HoldedTransientException: those are
    the Holded connector's and the connector stays in Base, which is the cycle Finance hit in A2
    (memory/architecture/vendor-connectors-own-sections.md).
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- ExpenseReportDto/ExpenseAttachmentDto (Instant) and ExpenseHoldedTimeline (LocalDate). -->
    <PackageReference Include="NodaTime" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
